# LEDGER MARKERS LIVE ON AT LEAST ONE GRAPH: {'?': 1, 'E': 1, 'y': 1, 'z': 1} of 8 markers
#   ^ SORTED, and that is DEFECT 20 (2026-10-04, found by the two-run byte check and by nothing else). `all_res` is a `Counter` whose insertion order is the order the markers were first seen, and it is fed by `py['residual'] | bd['residual']` -- a SET UNION, whose iteration order over STRINGS follows the per-process string hash and is therefore randomized by `PYTHONHASHSEED`. MEASURED: three consecutive runs of this oracle gave three answers, `{'y': 1, 'z': 1, 'q': 1, 'E': 1, '?': 2}` against `{'y': 1, 'z': 1, 'E': 1, 'q': 1, '?': 2}` against the first again, and the two-run sha256 check over `runs/graphcmp/D` caught it on `D0-coverage-census.txt` as the ONLY differing file out of 158.
#   It is the exact class the brief names: a COUNT that is right and an ORDER that is not, printed where a reader will read it as one line of fact. That is why 157 of 158 files were stable and this one was not.
#   AND THE CLASS HAD A SECOND MEMBER IN THIS FILE, WHICH THE PARAGRAPH ABOVE USED TO
#   DENY: 'Every OTHER iteration of a set in this file is already `sorted(...)`'. That sentence was
#   FALSE -- the `PY-BEND OPs DIFFER` row printed a SET LITERAL, `{py['ops'] ^ bd['ops']}` -- so the
#   sort and the correction are in ONE edit, because a comment that has stopped describing the code
#   is a pin that has stopped pinning. MEASURED, with no `bend` at all: three seeds gave
#   `{'PERMUTE','RANGE','REDUCE','COPY','ALLREDUCE','MUL'}`, `{'RANGE','COPY','MUL','REDUCE','PERMUTE','ALLREDUCE'}
#   and `{'MUL','COPY','ALLREDUCE','PERMUTE','REDUCE','RANGE'}` -- THREE renderings of ONE fact, and a
#   `repro` lane that reported `D0-coverage-census.txt: 2 runs DIFFER` on 1 of 196.
#   WHY SORTING AND NOT PINNING A SEED: a PIN IS A SEED AND A SORT IS A LAW. A seed fixes the order on
#   THIS interpreter and buys nothing on the next one, while the claim being protected -- 'the port and
#   CPython disagree' -- must survive a Python upgrade. An oracle whose set print follows the hash is a lane
#   that can never be green, and no amount of correctness in the port makes it so.
